3. Previous history of allergy to any component of monoclonal antibody or allergic constitution;
4. Uncontrolled cardiac symptoms or diseases, such as NYHA class II or higher Cardiac failure or left ventricular Ejection fraction (LVEF) \ Grade 2) occurred within 4 weeks before the first dose of the study drug, such as severe pneumonia, bacteraemia, and infectious complications requiring hospitalisation; Baseline chest imaging suggests active pneumonitis, symptoms and signs of infection within 2 weeks before the first dose of the study drug, or oral or intravenous antibiotic therapy is required for treatment (excluding the use of antibiotics for prophylaxis);
